<% content_for :title, "Docaru" %>
<% content_for :description, "Your household's documents, encrypted in your browser and reachable from anywhere. Sign in, or work out when to start a renewal without an account." %>

<%# The front door of the *application*, not the shopfront. The pitch lives on %>
<%# the marketing site, which deploys on its own schedule and is where the %>
<%# design effort goes; this page's job is to get a visitor to the thing they %>
<%# came for in one click. It used to open "Every document you own has a %>
<%# deadline", which sold the layer on top rather than the product. %>
<h1>Your documents, where you can reach them.</h1>

<p class="lede">
  Encrypted in your browser before they are uploaded, so nobody here can open them — and reachable
  from wherever you are when somebody asks for a copy.
</p>

<% if authenticated? %>
  <section class="answer">
    <p class="eyebrow">Signed in</p>
    <p class="headline"><%= link_to "Open the vault →", documents_path %></p>
    <p>
      Or see <%= link_to "what needs doing", dashboard_path %> — the documents with deadlines, and
      the dates you have to start.
    </p>
  </section>
<% else %>
  <section class="answer">
    <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
    <p class="headline"><%= link_to "Create a vault →", new_registration_path %></p>
    <p>
      Free for one person and a gigabyte, no card. Already have one?
      <%= link_to "Sign in", new_session_path %>.
    </p>
  </section>
<% end %>

<h2>Free, and no account needed</h2>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card">
    <h3><%= link_to "Work out when to start", calculator_path %></h3>
    <p class="note">
      Tell it what you have and when it expires. It counts back through processing times and the
      prerequisites you have not ordered yet, and gives you a date to begin. Nothing is stored.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3><%= link_to "Browse the playbooks", playbooks_path %></h3>
    <p class="note">
      <%= pluralize(@playbook_count, "playbook") %> across <%= pluralize(@rules.size, "document") %>
      and <%= pluralize(@country_count, "issuing country") %> — what each renewal needs, what it
      costs, and how long it really takes from where you are.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<p class="note">
  Reminders and playbooks are never paywalled. Somebody whose card fails while they are abroad is
  exactly the person most likely to need the alert.
</p>
